Z||000006||lou_dias||11-03-2000||09:34 AM||||At one time, I was thinking of starting a club in fall river and buying some property and hiring some mechanics to specialize in Fiero and do lots of kits and sell them and Warranty them at the shop (with rebuilt engines), but then my real career took off...<BR>I wanted to sell fully restored/upgraded Fieros...  Wrap around dashes, upgraded brakes and suspension.  Body Kits on them or stock....  Oh well, one can dream...<P>Anyway, the problem is right now, my free time is way too limited to be part of anything.  I'm buying a house, I do computer consulting on the side.  And other stuff.<P>The night where I don't usually have anything planned is Sunday night.  Once in a while I am free late Friday nights...  So I wouldn't be much in the way of a "good club member" type of guy.<P>You guys should come to Fall River and play laser tag and we could check out each other's rides some night.  I'm not anal about people driving my car unlike some other "car" people I know.  Just some warning.  The body is rough around the edges...  If you know somebody who could fix it up for me some Sunday afternoon, let me know after you see it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||11-03-2000||09:47 AM||||More babling...<P>I used to have an automatic GEO STORM GSI as a daily driver...in part for gas economy and in part because the BEAST was always in the shop and rarely running right.<P>Finally I shipped the beast to Ed Parks and had a rebuilt 3.4 put in along with all the custom parts I already had on the old engine.  Once I got it back, I sold the Geo...My highway fuel economy is 25mpg, so was the GEO's and I can no longer call it a beast because it's running great 14k miles later.  And it's running better ever since I switched to 87 octane gas (I think those Camaro engines have low compression pistons).  So it no longer became economical to the STORM anymore.<P>Now I think I need a second car again since in 5 months I've put on 14k miles, but I'm thinking Fiero 4 cyl w/5 speed...  I want to drive one though.  I heard they get close to 40 mpg...now that would make some economical sense and I wouldn't be betraying Fieros by getting a second car.  <BR>Anyone got one I can test drive?  Must be a 5 speed...||||reg||1
